12. The following point are arises for consideration is as follows;
1. Whether the prosecution proved beyond all reasonable doubt that on 07-06-2019 the accused No.1 had taken a hand loan of Rs. 5,00,000/- from CW1 namely Smt. Manjula at her residence bearing No.22 situated at Anjaneya Swamy Temple Road within the limits of J.C. Nagar Police Manjula vs Jinath Unnisa on 5 January, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/195319785/
3 Station, Bangalore by assuring to return the money within three months when CW1 demanded her money back, in the month of October 2019, accused No.2 entered the name of CW1 in Cheque No.501267 of SBI, Account No.20106378609 for Rs.2,00,000/- which was signed by accused No.1 in Urdu language with intention to cheat CW1 thereby resulted in commission of the offences punishable under U/s.467 and 468 read with Sec.34 of IPC?

Section 464 in The Indian Penal Code Making a false document.-- [A person is said to make a false document or false electronic record-- First --Who dishonestly or fradulently (a) makes, signs, seals or executes a document or part of a document;
(b) makes or transmits any electronic record or part of any electronic record;
(c) affixes any [electronic signature] on any electronic record;
